  "description": "CR 717.2a the level-2 trigger does not fire again when the Class goes from 2 to 3",
  "note": "'Becomes level 2' asks whether the level was below 2 and reached 2, which an equality on the resulting level or a bare 'reached at least 2' gets wrong. The level-2 section is still on at level 3, so the granted trigger exists throughout. The Class reaches level 2 with alice's graveyard empty (the trigger has no target and is removed, CR 603.3d), then Lightning Bolt is cast so an instant sits in her graveyard when the level-3 bar resolves; a trigger would bind it, its only candidate, and return it. The closing refused level-3 bar, with six Islands untapped to pay it, says the level really moved on to 3. The Haskell test wrote level 2 straight onto the Class.",
